<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fatimid Caliphate</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Fatimid, Fatimids</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Fatimid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">Caliphate</a> was an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ismailism">Ismaili</a> Shi'a caliphate founded in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-africa">North Africa</a> in 909 that conquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> in 969 and founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cairo">Cairo</a>. At its height it ruled North <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>, Egypt, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hejaz">Hejaz</a> and rivalled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbasid-caliphate">Abbasids</a>. It was weakened by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seljuk-empire">Seljuks</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusade">Crusades</a> and was abolished by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saladin">Saladin</a> in 1171, opening the way to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ayyubid-empire">Ayyubid Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fatimid-caliphate.jpg" alt="Fatimid Caliphate" width="320" height="183" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nourerrahmane (using file uploaded by Omar-toons as template) · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Fatimid_Caliphate.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
